---
import BlogLayout from "../../layouts/BlogLayout.astro";
import { getPublishedBlogPosts } from "../../core/blog/posts";
import { buildBlogIndexJsonLd } from "../../core/seo/jsonLd";
import { buildBlogIndexMeta } from "../../core/seo/meta";
import { siteConfig } from "../../core/site/config";
import danteHellEntry from "../../../content/dante_hell_entry.webp";

const meta = buildBlogIndexMeta(siteConfig.name);
const posts = getPublishedBlogPosts();
const jsonLd = buildBlogIndexJsonLd(meta, posts);
---

<BlogLayout meta={meta} jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <article class="blog-welcome">
    <header>
      <h1>All hope abandon, ye who enter in</h1>
      <p>Finally, I have my own little corner of the internet where I can show off, vent, or simply do a "brain dump." The topics I’ll be touching upon will certainly include the JVM (as I’ve been working with it for years), software architecture and system design in the broad sense, as well as the use of AI and its impact on our work. All of this is interwoven with my twisted sense of humor and a ton of memes.</p>
    </header>
    <div class="blog-index-list">
      {posts.map((post) => (
        <a class="blog-index-list__item" href={`/blog/${post.slug}/`}>
          <p>{post.publishedAt.toLocaleDateString("en", { day: "numeric", month: "short", year: "numeric" })}</p>
          <h2>{post.title}</h2>
          <span>{post.description}</span>
        </a>
      ))}
    </div>
    <p>I won’t waste your time with AI-generated slop; I promise that at least 80% of every post consists of my own writing, my own thoughts, and my own opinions..</p>
    <p>If you still want to read after that warning, welcome in.</p>
    <img class="blog-welcome__image" src={danteHellEntry.src} width={danteHellEntry.width} height={danteHellEntry.height} alt="The gate of Hell from Dante's Inferno, inscribed “Abandon every hope, all you who enter”" />
  </article>
</BlogLayout>
